From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rachapalli Bandi Jagadeesh <jagadeesh.rachapalli.bandi@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 12:43:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] vfio/pci: forward declare struct phys_vec in vfio_pci_core.h

On older kernels, <linux/types.h> does not define struct phys_vec.
vfio_pci_core.h names it in the always-present
vfio_pci_device_ops.get_dmabuf_phys() member and in the VFIO_PCI_DMABUF
disabled inline stubs, so the compiler warns.

Add a forward declaration alongside the other opaque struct
forward declarations. Only pointers to struct phys_vec are used in this
header, so a forward declaration is sufficient, and it is a harmless
no-op on newer kernels that already define the struct in types.h.

Warning:
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
warning: ‘struct phys_vec’ declared inside parameter list will not be visible
outside of this definition or declaration
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Signed-off-by: Rachapalli Bandi Jagadeesh <jagadeesh.rachapalli.bandi@intel.com>
---
 include/vfio/linux/vfio_pci_core.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/include/vfio/linux/vfio_pci_core.h b/include/vfio/linux/vfio_pci_core.h
index a8107ae..98fb112 100644
--- a/include/vfio/linux/vfio_pci_core.h
+++ b/include/vfio/linux/vfio_pci_core.h
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ struct vfio_pci_core_device;
 struct vfio_pci_region;
 struct p2pdma_provider;
 struct dma_buf_attachment;
+struct phys_vec;
 
 struct vfio_pci_eventfd {
 	struct eventfd_ctx	*ctx;
-- 
2.43.0

